1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,471
Tracebound is an evidence-first incident investigation agent built for the Open Agent

2
00:00:04,471 --> 00:00:05,208
Hackathon track,

3
00:00:05,208 --> 00:00:07,368
The Agent That Can Explain Why.

4
00:00:08,068 --> 00:00:09,234
During an incident,

5
00:00:09,234 --> 00:00:09,623
metrics,

6
00:00:09,623 --> 00:00:10,011
deployments,

7
00:00:10,011 --> 00:00:10,788
earlier incidents,

8
00:00:10,788 --> 00:00:13,120
and runbooks live in separate systems.

9
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:17,783
A plausible explanation is not enough unless responders can inspect what supports

10
00:00:17,783 --> 00:00:20,065
it and what contradicts the alternatives.

11
00:00:20,765 --> 00:00:25,148
This demo uses clearly labeled synthetic data and deterministic sample mode.

12
00:00:25,148 --> 00:00:29,930
Tracebound never presents the sample score as a production probability and never

13
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:30,677
executes remediation.

14
00:00:31,377 --> 00:00:33,177
When the investigation starts,

15
00:00:33,177 --> 00:00:38,575
every record enters a shared World Model with a stable content-derived identifier,

16
00:00:38,575 --> 00:00:39,925
a SHA-256 digest,

17
00:00:39,925 --> 00:00:40,825
source type,

18
00:00:40,825 --> 00:00:41,275
locator,

19
00:00:41,275 --> 00:00:42,175
observation time,

20
00:00:42,175 --> 00:00:43,474
and agent attribution.

21
00:00:44,174 --> 00:00:46,624
The same evidence cannot be silently duplicated.

22
00:00:46,624 --> 00:00:50,822
Every later claim links back to the exact records selected for that

23
00:00:50,822 --> 00:00:51,122
run.

24
00:00:51,822 --> 00:00:55,560
A Planner begins with a deliberately narrow four-record slice.

25
00:00:55,560 --> 00:01:00,545
The Investigator scores all three competing hypotheses from explicit support and contradiction

26
00:01:00,545 --> 00:01:00,910
links.

27
00:01:01,610 --> 00:01:05,289
The Challenger detects missing source types and uncovered alternatives.

28
00:01:05,289 --> 00:01:10,194
The Evaluator rejects that incomplete first pass and allows exactly one broader

29
00:01:10,194 --> 00:01:10,553
retry.

30
00:01:11,253 --> 00:01:12,530
On iteration two,

31
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:15,936
the investigation uses all seven records and stops.

32
00:01:15,936 --> 00:01:18,441
The bounded loop cannot spin indefinitely.

33
00:01:19,141 --> 00:01:22,598
The leading explanation is a payments timeout and retry cascade.

34
00:01:22,598 --> 00:01:26,748
A deployment reduced the timeout from three thousand to fifteen hundred milliseconds

35
00:01:26,748 --> 00:01:29,118
and raised retries from one to three.

36
00:01:29,818 --> 00:01:35,015
Payments p95 reached twenty-one hundred milliseconds and retry volume rose three point

37
00:01:35,015 --> 00:01:37,613
one times while traffic stayed flat.

38
00:01:37,613 --> 00:01:39,296
Database saturation remained normal.

39
00:01:39,996 --> 00:01:46,418
Tracebound therefore supports the timeout-and-retry cause while explicitly contradicting the traffic-spike and

40
00:01:46,418 --> 00:01:47,439
database-saturation alternatives.

41
00:01:48,139 --> 00:01:50,040
The recommended action is reversible:

42
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:51,562
canary the previous timeout,

43
00:01:51,562 --> 00:01:53,083
cap retries at one,

44
00:01:53,083 --> 00:01:57,216
and validate the change against the cited metrics before broad rollout.

45
00:01:57,916 --> 00:02:02,210
The repository includes a fail-closed Zetaris REST SQL adapter,

46
00:02:02,210 --> 00:02:04,118
Meterless World Model services,

47
00:02:04,118 --> 00:02:06,981
and a fail-closed Nightshift OpenAI-compatible adapter.

48
00:02:06,981 --> 00:02:09,793
NVIDIA can be configured behind Nightshift.

49
00:02:10,493 --> 00:02:13,508
Live sponsor verification is still pending account-owner setup,

50
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:17,277
so this recording does not claim that a real Zetaris,

51
00:02:17,277 --> 00:02:17,654
Nightshift,

52
00:02:17,654 --> 00:02:19,111
or NVIDIA call succeeded.

53
00:02:19,811 --> 00:02:22,382
Fresh release checks pass nine tests,

54
00:02:22,382 --> 00:02:23,668
TypeScript type checking,

55
00:02:23,668 --> 00:02:24,953
the production build,

56
00:02:24,953 --> 00:02:27,525
a dependency audit with zero vulnerabilities,

57
00:02:27,525 --> 00:02:29,239
an API smoke run,

58
00:02:29,239 --> 00:02:30,903
and a secret-pattern scan.

59
00:02:31,603 --> 00:02:33,653
Tracebound makes the investigation inspectable:

60
00:02:33,653 --> 00:02:34,883
what was selected,

61
00:02:34,883 --> 00:02:36,523
which alternatives were contradicted,

62
00:02:36,523 --> 00:02:38,164
why a retry happened,

63
00:02:38,164 --> 00:02:40,214
and which bounded action follows.

64
00:02:40,214 --> 00:02:41,034
The code,

65
00:02:41,034 --> 00:02:41,444
deck,

66
00:02:41,444 --> 00:02:42,264
architecture notes,

67
00:02:42,264 --> 00:02:47,184
and three synthetic cases are public at github dot com slash sidsri

68
00:02:47,184 --> 00:02:48,364
fourteen slash tracebound.
